- The draft's "no genuine video exists" claim is well supported: the YouTube "recordings" self-disclose as AI TTS and the "exclusive interview" captions open as a two-host AI narration.

**Largest unresolved evidence gap:** the authenticity of the May 20, 2026 transcript itself. The title phrase, the signature "118 points" section, the pricing scene, the team-stability fear beat, and the curiosity-vs-greatest-return anomaly all rest on a speaker-unlabeled ASR document that DeepSeek has neither confirmed nor denied, vouched for only by one anonymous investing institution via NBD. A close second: the draft's own falsification test (a post-IPO price hike) may already be partly answerable — August 2026 trade headlines reference DeepSeek API price-hike signals, which I did not verify and flagged for the evaluators.
